From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: himax-spi: pressure_enabled 跟着轴走；contacts_log 加 zone_area 列

**① `pressure_enabled` 的默认值是个逻辑缺陷，不是调参项。**

`disable_pressure=0` 时驱动注册 `ABS_MT_TOUCH_MAJOR` / `ABS_MT_PRESSURE` 两个轴，
但 `hx_algo_init_defaults()` 把 `pressure_enabled` 无条件设成 `false`，于是
`himax_report_tracked_state()` 往这两个轴里填的是**常数**（1 和 4095）——
每个触点都成了"针尖"，**比不注册这两个轴还糟**。实机 `#23` 起来时正是这个状态，
要手动 `echo 1 > algo/pressure_enabled` 才对。

改成在 probe 里 `ts->algo->pressure_enabled = !disable_pressure`：轴存在就报真值。
sysfs 旋钮保留，仍可运行时改。

**② `contacts_log` 加 `zone_area` 列 —— 今晚缺的正是它。**

实机量过（案卷 #116）：`ct->area`（"≥峰值一半"的格子数）纯指尖是 8–20，
手掌压屏时活下来的触点是 5–21，**完全重叠**。原因是构造性的：手掌碎块各有局部峰值，
50% 等高线和指尖差不多大。能分开两者的是**连通域面积**（在绝对阈值 `macro_threshold`
上的 8-连通区域，`peaks[].zone_area`），可它没被记进触点里。

给 `struct hx_contact` 加 `zone_area`，`hx_expand_and_resolve()` 从对应峰值抄过来，
出生记录随之多一列。有了它才能回答"`palm_area_threshold` 该从 50 降到多少"。

案卷：`docs/stage4-findings.md` #116。
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c
@@ -1126,16 +1126,17 @@
 	struct hx_algo *algo = ((struct himax_ts_data *)dev_get_drvdata(dev))->algo;
 	int n = 0, k;
 
-	n += sysfs_emit_at(buf, n, "  seq      x      y  area   signal edge\n");
+	n += sysfs_emit_at(buf, n, "  seq      x      y  area  zone   signal edge\n");
 	for (k = 0; k < HX_NEWLOG; k++) {
 		struct hx_newlog *lg =
 			&algo->newlog[(algo->newlog_head + k) % HX_NEWLOG];
 
 		if (!lg->seq)
 			continue;
-		n += sysfs_emit_at(buf, n, "%5u %6d %6d %5u %8d %4u\n",
+		n += sysfs_emit_at(buf, n, "%5u %6d %6d %5u %5u %8d %4u\n",
 					   lg->seq, lg->x, lg->y, lg->area,
-					   lg->signal_sum, lg->is_edge ? 1 : 0);
+					   lg->zone_area, lg->signal_sum,
+					   lg->is_edge ? 1 : 0);
 	}
 	return n;
 }
@@ -1627,6 +1628,13 @@
 	if (!ts->algo)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	hx_algo_init_defaults(ts->algo);
+	/*
+	 * With the TOUCH_MAJOR/PRESSURE axes registered, reporting the constants
+	 * (1 and 4095) that pressure_enabled=false selects is never what anyone
+	 * wants -- every contact becomes a needle point.  Follow the axes: report
+	 * real values whenever the axes exist.  Still writable through sysfs.
+	 */
+	ts->algo->pressure_enabled = !disable_pressure;
 
 	spin_lock_init(&ts->irq_lock);
 	mutex_init(&ts->op_lock);
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
@@ -1005,6 +1005,14 @@
 		clean = hx_expand_single_peak(algo, i, ct);
 		if (!clean)
 			hx_local_centroid(algo, i, ct);
+		/*
+		 * ct->area is measured at half the peak and so is roughly the same
+		 * for a fingertip and for a fragment of a palm (measured on the
+		 * panel: 8-20 vs 5-21 cells).  The macro-zone area at the absolute
+		 * threshold is the quantity that can tell them apart; carry it along
+		 * so the contact log can show it.
+		 */
+		ct->zone_area = algo->peaks[i].zone_area;
 
 		/*
 		 * Per-contact palm test.  ct->area counts only cells at or above
@@ -1267,6 +1275,8 @@
 			lg->area       = j < algo->contact_count ?
 					     algo->contacts[j].area : 0;
 			lg->signal_sum = trk->signal_sum;
+			lg->zone_area  = j < algo->contact_count ?
+					     algo->contacts[j].zone_area : 0;
 			lg->is_edge    = j < algo->contact_count &&
 					     algo->contacts[j].is_edge;
 			if (lg->is_edge)
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.h b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.h
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.h
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.h
@@ -54,6 +54,7 @@
 	u16  area;
 	s32  signal_sum;
 	bool is_edge;
+	u16  zone_area;   /* area of the macro-zone this contact came from */
 };
 
 /**
@@ -145,6 +146,7 @@
 	u16  area;
 	s32  signal_sum;
 	bool is_edge;
+	u16  zone_area;
 };
 
 /**
